CORE
main.c
--no-standard-checks
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* known object: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] .* integer address: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A program that declares __CPROVER_shadow_memory_incomplete learns that
set_field or get_field could not resolve an object, rather than losing the
field value silently.
